{"format":1,"seq":72,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing whether the durable entry should keep treating pi-durable as optional versus directly importing fitImage from pi-durable/images/fit, since that would tie it to a peer dependency of ^1.6.0 and introduce version coupling I'm not sure is worth it.\n\nMy plan is to do the version upgrades first and run tsc to see what breaks before deciding on improvements: bump Pi to 1.6.0, oxfmt to 0.80.0, oxlint to 1.95.0, and vitest/coverage to 5.1.1, while keeping typebox at 1.3.27 since Pi pins it and staying on TS 6 since TS 7's API isn't compatible. I also need to check whether typescript is actually used at runtime for transpilation and whether pi-codemode depends on it.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01NDnvMs97yvS47dCGMRdEDX","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Install Pi 1.6.0, oxfmt 0.80, oxlint 1.95, vitest 5.1.1\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`npm view @earendil-works/pi-codemode@1.6.0 dependencies peerDependencies --json; npm view @earendil-works/pi-durable@1.6.0 dependencies peerDependencies --json; npm install --save-exact @earendil-works/pi-codemode@1.6.0 oxfmt@0.80.0 && npm install --save-dev --save-exact @earendil-works/chord@1.6.0 @earendil-works/pi-ai@1.6.0 @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@1.6.0 @earendil-works/pi-durable@1.6.0 @earendil-works/pi-tui@1.6.0 oxlint@1.95.0 && npm install --save-dev vitest@^5.1.1 @vitest/coverage-v8@^5.1.1 2>&1 | tail -15; git diff --stat`, { timeoutMs: 280000 });\n  return r.stdout.slice(-6000) + r.stderr.slice(-3000);\n}","timeoutMs":290000}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":855,"cacheRead":34707,"cacheWrite":5023,"totalTokens":40587,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvide